\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces (left) Deep Concept Reasoner (DCR) generates fuzzy logic rules using neural models on concept embeddings. Then DCR executes the rule using the concept truth degrees to evaluate the rule symbolically. (right) Schema of DCR modules: first neural models $\phi $ and $\psi $ generate the rule, and then the rule is executed symbolically.}}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:f4}{{4}{5}{(left) Deep Concept Reasoner (DCR) generates fuzzy logic rules using neural models on concept embeddings. Then DCR executes the rule using the concept truth degrees to evaluate the rule symbolically. (right) Schema of DCR modules: first neural models $\phi $ and $\psi $ generate the rule, and then the rule is executed symbolically}{figure.4}{}}
